ان خاطر يثبت له المتصفح. بعدين كده تاني حاجة اللي هو Get session ويبقى جنبيه صح، Open SSL أو SSH ده عشان يجيب له الكود بتاع الـ API Key ده بالنسبة للسيرفر. وبرضه لما تعمل الحتة دي يسمع في الـ Environment، تمام أنت ممكن تقرأ الـ Folder يعني الـ Readme Folder، الـ Readme بتاع الـ Folder وبرضه وزرار Start Start الـ Start اسمه ده الـ Start اللي هو السيرفر. طيب قشطا طالما طالما الـ requirements صح وطالما الـ Get session صح يبقى موجود بره تحت الضبط تحت بره اللي هو أول ما يفتح الـ Application تشغيل السيرفر على طول بدل ما يخش على إعدادات السيرفر. بدل ما يخش على الإعدادات يبقى فيه برضه على الجنب كده تشغيل السيرفر، فيشتغل السيرفر في الخلفية أو حاجة مش ظاهرة، أهم حاجة الـ Terminal ما يظهرش. تمام وتشغيل السيرفر ده يتقلب اللي هو إيقاف السيرفر عشان خاطر لما يخلص يعمل إيقاف، أو لو مش هيعمل إيقاف كده لما يقفل الـ Application كل حاجه الـ Process بتحصل لها Kill يعني، بس كل حركة فيها Save. تمام كل حركة فيها Save وكده كده أنا هبقى أظبطه له يعني. حتى الآن يعني ده اللي احنا متفقين عليه. ممكن نعدل برضه قدام يعني على حسب بقى صاحبي لما يلاقي حاجة من اللي هو احنا عملناها مش عاجباه. \"\n\nSelection:\n>اسم التطبيق: إيه الاسم اللي تحبه يظهر على الأيقونة والـ Title Bar؟ (مثلاً: \"مطابق الأدوية\" أو \"Pharmacy Matcher\" أو اسم تاني؟)\n\nComment: \"مش عارف والله، شوف كدا اسم جذاب وبسيط، مثلا Pharmacy Matcher، ماشي ما فيش مشكلة عليه. \"\n\nSelection:\n>الـ MSEMAX: صاحبك هيحتاج يشغل سيرفر MSEMAX على جهازه عشان الموديل يشتغل، ولا إنت هتسيبه شغال على جهازك وهو يتصل بيك عن بعد؟ لأن ده هيأثر على إعدادات الـ API URL في التطبيق.\n\nComment: \"انا هنقل المشروع بتاعك اللي احنا هنعمله، وانت هتقول لي انقل ايه بالظبط، وهنقل برضه السيرفر بتاع ال ام اس اي ده. \"\n<USER_REQUEST>\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-22T01:15:56+03:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":319,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:15:56Z","content":"ممتاز! فهمت كل التفاصيل الجديدة. هبدأ أنفذ فوراً. خليني أعمل Task List وأبدأ أبني التطبيق.","thinking":"The user has approved the plan with additional requirements. Let me summarize what they want:\n\n1. **App Name**: \"Pharmacy Matcher\" is fine\n2. **MSEMAX**: Will be copied to the friend's machine alongside the project\n3. **New Requirements - Settings Page**:\n   - A Settings page accessible from the main screen\n   - Settings for APIs (Unstructured.io API key, Model provider - local MSEMAX or others)\n   - MSEMAX Server Management within the app:\n     - \"Setup Requirements\" button (installs pip requirements + `playwright install` for browser) with a checkmark\n     - \"Get Session\" button (runs get_session.py to get the API key/session) with a checkmark\n     - \"Start Server\" button that runs the server silently in the background, toggling to \"Stop Server\" while active, with a matching quick-access button on the main screen\n     - Closing the app should kill all background processes, and every action should auto-save\n\nI should update the implementation plan to reflect these additions and then move into building it out.\n\nI'm now sketching the architecture: a pywebview desktop window with an HTML/CSS/JS single-page frontend, a Python backend exposed through pywebview's JS API, SQLite for history storage, and PyInstaller for packaging into an EXE. I'm breaking this into components -- the main app entry point, a backend API class, a database manager, a server subprocess manager, and the HTML template -- planning to split this large build into tasks handled by subagents.\n\nI'm considering splitting the work using subagents—one for the backend files, one for the frontend, while I handle app.py, setup.bat, run.bat, and overall coordination, though I need to think through the dependencies between these pieces first.\n\nThe frontend and backend need a defined API contract before I split off work, so I'll decide that first, then simply proceed to build files myself step by step in the right order. I also need to check the existing MSEMAX folder structure, including its FastAPI server and session capture script, to see what needs to be integrated.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the backend API surface: starting new matching processes, checking status and results, opening the Excel output or folder, applying finalized reviews, pulling process history and details, and saving settings.\n\nI also need endpoints for MSEMAX integration—installing its requirements, generating a session, and starting/stopping/checking its background server.\n\nGiven the scope, I think it's best to parallelize this work with subagents. I'll define a \"desktop-app-builder\" subagent, build out the task list first, then launch multiple instances to tackle different parts simultaneously.\n\nThe quickest path forward is to update the implementation plan and task list, then start building the core files myself while delegating the large HTML/CSS/JS frontend work to subagents.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Task checklist for building the Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App with all screens, settings, MSEMAX integration, and history.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App — Tasks\n\n## Phase 1: Core Infrastructure\n- [ ] Create `desktop_app/` folder structure\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/database.py` — SQLite history manager\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/server_manager.py` — MSEMAX process manager\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/backend.py` — Python API bridge for UI\n\n## Phase 2: Frontend UI\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/templates/index.html` — Full SPA (Home, New, Results, History, Settings)\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/static/style.css` — RTL professional styling\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/static/app.js` — Frontend logic + API calls\n\n## Phase 3: App Entry & Launch\n- [ ] Build `desktop_app/app.py` — pywebview entry point\n- [ ] Create `setup.bat` — installs requirements + creates desktop shortcut\n- [ ] Create `run.bat` — launches app without Terminal\n- [ ] Install `pywebview` dependency\n\n## Phase 4: Testing & Polish\n- [ ] End-to-end test: New → Submit → Review → Finalize\n- [ ] Test History persistence\n- [ ] Test MSEMAX server start/stop\n","Description":"Task tracking for Desktop App build","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\task.md","toolAction":"Creating task list","toolSummary":"Task checklist"}}]}
