{"step_index":322,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:16:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T01:16:47+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T01:16:48+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///D:/AI_Engineer/MSEMAX/app.py`\nTotal Lines: 806\nTotal Bytes: 30198\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: MSEMAX Gateway — FastAPI Server (Main Application)\n3: \n4: A high-performance, OpenAI-compatible API gateway that proxies chat completion\n5: requests through ChatGPT's backend API. Provides streaming and non-streaming\n6: responses with automatic metadata sanitization.\n7: \n8: Core responsibilities:\n9:   - Accept OpenAI-format requests (POST /v1/chat/completions)\n10:   - Authenticate via Bearer token\n11:   - Enforce rate limits (per-IP) and concurrency limits (global semaphore)\n12:   - Resolve chat-requirements (POW challenges, turnstile tokens)\n13:   - Stream responses back in OpenAI SSE format\n14:   - Strip ChatGPT metadata noise (entity tags, citations, image groups)\n15: \n16: Author: Mohamed (MSEMAX)\n17: License: MIT\n18: \"\"\"\n19: \n20: import os\n21: import re\n22: import json\n23: import uuid\n24: import time\n25: import codecs\n26: import asyncio\n27: import logging\n28: from typing import AsyncGenerator, Optional, Any\n29: from fastapi import FastAPI, Request, HTTPException, Depends\n30: from fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse, JSONResponse\n31: from fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n32: from curl_cffi.requests import AsyncSession\n33: from pydantic import BaseModel\n34: from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n35: from slowapi import Limiter, _rate_limit_exceeded_handler\n36: from slowapi.util import get_remote_address\n37: from slowapi.errors import RateLimitExceeded\n38: \n39: # Import the POW solver module\n40: from pow_solver import solve_pow_async, get_pool, shutdown_pool\n41: import warnings\n42: warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning, module=\"curl_cffi\")\n43: logging.basicConfig(\n44:     level=logging.INFO,\n45:     format=\"%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s\"\n46: )\n47: logger = logging.getLogger(\"msemax.api\")\n48: \n49: try:\n50:     from dotenv import load_dotenv\n51:     load_dotenv()\n52: except ImportError:\n53:     pass\n54: \n55: def get_env_or_raise(key: str) -> str:\n56:     val = os.environ.get(key)\n57:     if val is None:\n58:         raise RuntimeError(f\"{key} environment variable is required. Please add it to your .env file.\")\n59:     return val\n60: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
