{"step_index":327,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:17:02Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Subagents":[{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the following 3 Python files for the Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App at d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\.\n\n## File 1: desktop_app/database.py\n\nSQLite database manager for process history. Use a single file `data/history.db`.\n\n```python\nimport sqlite3\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nDATA_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / 'data'\nDB_PATH = DATA_DIR / 'history.db'\nPROCESSES_DIR = DATA_DIR / 'processes'\n```\n\nClass `HistoryDB`:\n- `__init__()` — creates DATA_DIR, PROCESSES_DIR, and the DB tables if not exist\n- Tables:\n  - `processes`: id (TEXT PRIMARY KEY like 'PROC-001'), created_at (TEXT ISO format), status (TEXT: 'processing'|'completed'|'reviewing'), shortage_files (TEXT JSON list of filenames), warehouse_files (TEXT JSON list of filenames), total_shortages (INT), matched_count (INT), not_found_count (INT), review_count (INT), output_file (TEXT path to results xlsx)\n- `get_next_id()` — returns next PROC-XXX id\n- `create_process(shortage_filenames: list[str], warehouse_filenames: list[str]) -> str` — creates a new process entry with status='processing', returns process_id. Also creates the process folder structure: `PROCESSES_DIR / process_id / {input_shortages, input_warehouses, output}`\n- `update_process(process_id, **kwargs)` — updates any columns\n- `get_process(process_id) -> dict` — returns process as dict\n- `get_all_processes() -> list[dict]` — returns all processes ordered by created_at DESC\n- `delete_process(process_id)` — deletes process record and its folder\n- `get_process_dir(process_id) -> Path` — returns the process folder path\n\n## File 2: desktop_app/server_manager.py\n\nManages the MSEMAX server as a background subprocess.\n\n```python\nimport subprocess\nimport os\nimport signal\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n```\n\nClass `MSEMAXServerManager`:\n- `__init__(msemax_dir: str)` — stores the MSEMAX directory path, `self.process = None`\n- `is_running() -> bool` — checks if the subprocess is alive\n- `start() -> dict` — starts `python app.py` inside the MSEMAX dir as a background subprocess with `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` flag (so no terminal shows). Sets `cwd` to msemax_dir. Uses the same Python executable. Returns `{\"success\": True/False, \"message\": str}`. If already running, returns success with message 'already running'.\n- `stop() -> dict` — kills the subprocess and all children using `taskkill /F /T /PID`. Returns `{\"success\": True/False, \"message\": str}`\n- `install_requirements() -> dict` — runs `pip install -r requirements.txt` in msemax_dir, captures output. Returns `{\"success\": bool, \"output\": str}`\n- `run_get_session() -> dict` — runs `python get_session.py` in msemax_dir. This is interactive (opens a browser), so run it visible. Returns `{\"success\": bool, \"output\": str}`. NOTE: This needs to run with a visible window since it opens a browser for login.\n- `install_playwright() -> dict` — runs `playwright install chromium`, captures output. Returns `{\"success\": bool, \"output\": str}`\n- `get_status() -> dict` — returns `{\"running\": bool, \"pid\": int|None}`\n- `cleanup()` — kills the process if running (call on app exit)\n\nIMPORTANT: On Windows, use `subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW = 0x08000000` for hiding the terminal. Use `subprocess.Popen` not `subprocess.run` for the server start.\n\n## File 3: desktop_app/backend.py\n\nThis is the Python API class that `pywebview` exposes to JavaScript. Every public method becomes callable from JS via `window.pywebview.api.method_name()`.\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport threading\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Add project root to path\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n```\n\nClass `API`:\n- `__init__(window=None)` — stores window ref, initializes `HistoryDB`, `MSEMAXServerManager`, loads settings from `data/settings.json`\n- **Settings:**\n  - `get_settings() -> dict` — returns settings dict: `{unstructured_api_key, local_api_url, local_api_key, local_model, msemax_dir}`\n  - `save_settings(settings_json: str) -> dict` — saves to `data/settings.json`, returns `{\"success\": True}`\n- **MSEMAX Server:**\n  - `start_server() -> dict` — delegates to server_manager.start()\n  - `stop_server() -> dict` — delegates to server_manager.stop()\n  - `get_server_status() -> dict` — delegates to server_manager.get_status()\n  - `setup_msemax_requirements() -> dict` — delegates to server_manager.install_requirements() + install_playwright()\n  - `run_get_session() -> dict` — delegates to server_manager.run_get_session()\n- **Process:**\n  - `start_process(shortage_paths_json: str, warehouse_paths_json: str) -> dict` — Main method. Parses the JSON lists of file paths. Creates a new process in DB. Copies input files to process folder. Runs the matching engine (imports from src.config, src.extract, src.fast_match, src.output). Updates DB with results. Returns `{\"success\": True, \"process_id\": str, \"summary\": dict}`. Run the actual matching in a thread to not block the UI, and use `window.evaluate_js()` to send progress updates.\n  - `get_process_result(process_id: str) -> dict` — returns process details from DB\n- **File Operations:**\n  - `open_excel(process_id: str) -> dict` — opens the output Excel file with `os.startfile()`\n  - `open_folder(process_id: str) -> dict` — opens the output folder in Explorer with `os.startfile()`\n  - `open_file(filepath: str) -> dict` — opens any file with `os.startfile()`\n- **Review:**\n  - `apply_reviews(process_id: str) -> dict` — reads the Excel file, processes rows with decisions (✅/❌), moves them, removes processed rows from review sheet, saves. Returns `{\"success\": True, \"matched\": int, \"rejected\": int, \"remaining\": int}`\n- **History:**\n  - `get_history() -> str` — returns JSON string of all processes\n  - `get_process_details(process_id: str) -> str` — returns JSON string of process details including file lists\n  - `delete_process(process_id: str) -> dict` — deletes a process\n- **Cleanup:**\n  - `on_closing()` — stops server, cleans up resources\n\nIMPORTANT for `start_process`: \n1. Parse the file paths from JSON strings\n2. Create process in DB \n3. Copy files to process directory\n4. Load config (update config with current settings before running)\n5. Run the matching pipeline (read_input_files, FastCoordinator.process, write_results_excel)\n6. The output file should go to the process's output folder\n7. Update DB with summary stats\n8. Return the result\n\nFor `apply_reviews`:\n1. Load the output Excel file using openpyxl\n2. Read the 'يحتاج مراجعة' sheet\n3. For each row:\n   - Column A (index 0) = 'القرار (اختر)'\n   - If '✅ مطابق': move to warehouse sheet, mark for deletion\n   - If '❌ غير مطابق': move to 'لم يُعثر عليه', mark for deletion  \n   - If empty: leave as is\n4. Delete processed rows (bottom-up to avoid index shift)\n5. Save the Excel file\n6. Return counts\n\nAlso create an empty `desktop_app/__init__.py`.","Role":"Backend Python builder","TypeName":"desktop-builder"},{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the frontend files for the Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App at d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\.\n\nThe app uses `pywebview` which means JavaScript calls Python via `window.pywebview.api.method_name()`. All methods return promises.\n\n## File 1: desktop_app/templates/index.html\n\nA complete Single Page Application with these screens:\n\n### Screen 1: Home (id='screen-home')\n- App logo/title: 'Pharmacy Matcher' with Arabic subtitle 'نظام مطابقة الأدوية'\n- 4 main buttons in a grid:\n  1. 🆕 عملية جديدة (New) → shows screen-new\n  2. 📜 السجل (History) → shows screen-history  \n  3. ⚙️ الإعدادات (Settings) → shows screen-settings\n  4. ❌ خروج (Exit) → calls window.pywebview.api.on_closing() then closes\n- Server status indicator at top-left: green dot + 'السيرفر يعمل' or red dot + 'السيرفر متوقف'\n- Quick button next to it: 'تشغيل السيرفر' / 'إيقاف السيرفر'\n\n### Screen 2: New Process (id='screen-new')\n- Two drop zones:\n  1. 'ملفات المخازن (PDF / Excel / JSON)' — accepts multiple files, shows list of selected files\n  2. 'ملفات النواقص (PDF / Excel)' — accepts multiple files, shows list of selected files\n- File input buttons (for clicking, not just drag & drop)\n- ▶️ Submit button (disabled until both have files)\n- Progress area (hidden until submit): spinning animation + status text\n- 🔙 Back button\n\n### Screen 3: Results (id='screen-results')\n- Summary cards at top: total shortages, matched, not found, needs review (with numbers and percentages)\n- 4 action buttons:\n  1. 📊 فتح ملف الإكسيل — calls `pywebview.api.open_excel(processId)`\n  2. 📁 فتح مكان الملف — calls `pywebview.api.open_folder(processId)`  \n  3. ✏️ تنفيذ تعديلات المراجعة — calls `pywebview.api.apply_reviews(processId)`, shows result toast\n  4. 🔙 الرئيسية — goes back to home\n- A note text explaining the workflow: 'افتح ملف الإكسيل، راجع شيت المراجعة، اختر ✅ أو ❌، احفظ، ثم اضغط تنفيذ التعديلات'\n\n### Screen 4: History (id='screen-history')\n- List of process cards, each showing:\n  - Process ID + date/time\n  - Status badge (completed/reviewing)\n  - Stats: matched/not found/review counts\n  - Click to open → shows screen-results for that process\n- If no history: empty state message\n- 🔙 Back button\n\n### Screen 5: Settings (id='screen-settings')\n- **Section: إعدادات الـ APIs**\n  - Input: Unstructured.io API Key\n  - Input: Local API URL (default: http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions)\n  - Input: Local API Key\n  - Input: Model name (default: gpt-4o-mini)\n  - Save button\n- **Section: إعدادات سيرفر MSEMAX**\n  - Input: MSEMAX Directory path (with browse button)\n  - Button: 'تثبيت المتطلبات (Requirements + Playwright)' with ✅ indicator\n  - Button: 'تجديد الجلسة (Get Session)' with ✅ indicator  \n  - Button: 'تشغيل / إيقاف السيرفر' with status indicator\n- 🔙 Back button\n\n### Navigation:\n- Use a simple function `showScreen(screenId)` that hides all screens and shows the requested one\n- Global variable `currentProcessId` to track which process is being viewed\n\n### HTML Structure:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang='ar' dir='rtl'>\n<head>\n  <meta charset='UTF-8'>\n  <title>Pharmacy Matcher</title>\n  <link rel='stylesheet' href='../static/style.css'>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- All screens here -->\n  <script src='../static/app.js'></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nIMPORTANT: For file inputs, use regular `<input type='file'>` with `multiple` attribute. pywebview on Windows supports file dialogs. Wrap them in styled labels for the drop zone look. Use `webkitRelativePath` or just grab `file.name` and send paths.\n\nActually, since pywebview provides file paths differently, for file selection, add buttons that call a JS function which will use `<input type='file'>` to let user pick files. Store the selected File objects and their paths. When submitting, we'll need the actual file paths. In pywebview, we can use `window.pywebview.api.select_files(type)` to open a native file dialog. Add these methods to the backend API calls.\n\nFor drag and drop: use standard HTML5 drag and drop. However, getting the full file path from dropped files is not possible in standard web APIs. So instead, use buttons that trigger file input, and for each zone show the list of selected file names. The actual file paths will be captured by the input element.\n\nREVISED APPROACH: Use `<input type='file' multiple>` elements. When files are selected, display the file names in the drop zone. When Submit is pressed, send the file paths to the Python backend. In pywebview, `input.files[i].name` gives the filename but NOT the full path. So we need to use pywebview's `create_file_dialog` instead.\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. User clicks 'اختيار ملفات المخازن' button\n2. JS calls `await window.pywebview.api.select_files('warehouse')` \n3. Python opens a native file dialog, returns list of full paths\n4. JS displays the file names in the UI\n5. On Submit, JS sends the stored paths to `start_process()`\n\nAdd these to the backend API:\n- `select_files(file_type: str) -> str` — opens native file dialog, returns JSON list of selected file paths\n\n## File 2: desktop_app/static/style.css\n\nProfessional, modern CSS:\n- RTL direction\n- Dark sidebar or clean white design\n- Color scheme: primary=#00695C (teal), accent=#FF6F00 (amber), bg=#F5F5F5\n- Card-based layout with shadows\n- Smooth transitions between screens\n- Responsive within the window\n- Nice drop zones with dashed borders\n- Status badges (green for matched, red for not found, orange for review)\n- Toast notifications\n- Spinning loader animation\n- Google Fonts: use 'Cairo' for Arabic text (import from Google Fonts CDN)\n- Buttons with hover effects\n- File list items with X to remove\n\n## File 3: desktop_app/static/app.js\n\nJavaScript logic:\n- `showScreen(id)` — hides all `.screen` elements, shows the one with matching id\n- `currentProcessId` — global var\n- `selectedShortageFiles` / `selectedWarehouseFiles` — arrays of file paths\n- File selection functions that call `pywebview.api.select_files(type)`\n- `submitProcess()` — calls `pywebview.api.start_process(...)`, shows progress, then shows results\n- `openExcel()` — calls `pywebview.api.open_excel(currentProcessId)`\n- `openFolder()` — calls `pywebview.api.open_folder(currentProcessId)`\n- `applyReviews()` — calls `pywebview.api.apply_reviews(currentProcessId)`, shows toast with counts\n- `loadHistory()` — calls `pywebview.api.get_history()`, renders the list\n- `viewProcess(processId)` — loads process details and shows results screen\n- `loadSettings()` / `saveSettings()` — settings management\n- `startServer()` / `stopServer()` — server management\n- `setupRequirements()` / `getSession()` — MSEMAX setup\n- `updateServerStatus()` — polls server status every 5 seconds, updates the indicator\n- `showToast(message, type)` — shows a temporary notification (success/error)\n- Wait for `window.pywebview.api` to be ready before doing anything:\n```js\nwindow.addEventListener('pywebviewready', function() {\n  loadSettings();\n  updateServerStatus();\n  setInterval(updateServerStatus, 5000);\n});\n```\n\nMake sure ALL pywebview API calls use `await` and are wrapped in try/catch for error handling.\nMake sure the UI is beautiful and professional — this is for a pharmacy business.","Role":"Frontend UI builder","TypeName":"desktop-builder"}],"toolAction":"Launching parallel builders","toolSummary":"Launch builder subagents"}}]}
